#1 Indexed Color PSD and PSB fixtures, authored by Adobe Photoshop 2025 26.10.0
(scripts/photoshop-probe/indexed_psd_take.py, take1, run 20261024T025614Z-9e90f7e4;
receipts in ~/devel/doctored-fixtures/photoshop/indexed-psd-547/take1).

Each file is one of the runner's PNG scenes, opened in Photoshop and converted by ONE
Image > Mode > Indexed Color (CnvM IndC: Palette Exact, Forced None, Transparency true for
exact_t only, DialogModes.NO). Photoshop then saved it as a PSD (PhotoshopSaveOptions, layers,
profile embedded) and, for exact and exact_t, as a PSB (the largeDocumentFormat save
descriptor, which embeds no profile: those two carry resource 1041 and no 1039).

  exact.psd, exact.psb       24 x 16, six 4-px bands (200,30,30) (30,160,60) (40,60,200)
                             (230,200,40) (20,20,20) (128,128,128); 6 entries, no t
  exact_t.psd, exact_t.psb   the same with x >= 20 clear; 5 opaque entries + t = 5 (white)
  full256.psd                16 x 16, pixel (x, y) = (17x, 17y, 128); 256 entries, Raw composite

photoshop.json holds, for each file, its sha256, bytes, document row, mode, count, palette,
transparent index, index rows and layout (as the runner's reader reads it).

What the layout says, which is the writer's spec (core/src/indexed_psd.rs):
- the header declares ONE channel, transparent index or not;
- the 768-byte table is planar and zero-padded past the count;
- 1046 (the count) and 1047 are in every file: 1047 is 0xFFFF with no transparent index;
- the layer-and-mask section holds NO layer record (layer information length 0, then a
  global mask and the tail blocks CAI, OCIO, GenI, FMsk, cinf), and Photoshop reopens every
  file, exact_t included, as one Background layer;
- the composite is RLE except full256's, which is Raw.

Read by core/tests/indexed_psd_photoshop.rs, which SKIPs when this folder is absent.
